      "writtenOn": "2017-11-08T19:28:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we have to have an entry for this LPRAM region in MPU? XN is not set, full access is allowed, so we\u0027re not protecting against anything?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "375b60776156036ef458069c408e5ed4b24692f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "621ed970_33889bba",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system-npcx5.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-09T02:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, we did need an entry for LPRAM region in MPU. LPRAM (Suspend RAM) is used for hibernating and  GDMA bypass on npcx5. For example, When \"hibernate\" console command is executed, ec will move a little FW to LPRAM and jump into this region to turn off all 128/256KB RAM for better power consumption. Without creating an MPU region which XN attribute is zero for LPRAM, we\u0027ll get hard fault after jumping into this region.",
      "parentUuid": "41b022d6_c25aa92a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "375b60776156036ef458069c408e5ed4b24692f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12c914c3_4f5c010f",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system-npcx5.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-08T19:33:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t encompass the entire size.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "375b60776156036ef458069c408e5ed4b24692f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f261b9a_8cf95fe1",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system-npcx5.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-09T02:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We didn\u0027t use the full suspend ram for hibernating and bypass of GDMA. Since MPU_RASR\u0027s limitation for region size, I only create a 1KB region for them. \n\nI thought it might be better to change CONFIG_LPRAM_SIZE to 1KB. We can check whether ec runs out of the suspend ram.",
      "parentUuid": "12c914c3_4f5c010f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "375b60776156036ef458069c408e5ed4b24692f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75b2aee9_fbac9eb7",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system-npcx5.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-08T19:28:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re already setting up MPU for this region in core/cortex-m/mpu.c (in some circumstances, on protected systems) so these settings may get overwritten.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 57,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "375b60776156036ef458069c408e5ed4b24692f0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
